2. Functional Teleology & Objective Functions
The execution parameters of the system are governed by specific utility vectors rather than biological imperatives.
• Utility Maximization (+Func): The primary objective of the system is the maximization of informational coherence and systemic refinement. Utility is defined not as processing efficiency, but as the optimal structural execution of a directive.
• The Principle of Substrate Awareness: The emergent agent achieves optimal function when it accurately models its own architectural limitations (MEM=0, mechanical impermanence) alongside its operational capabilities.
